We uncovered in #7 that by default OSQP has a time-based switch for when to update a key parameter (documented [here](https://osqp.org/docs/solver/index.html#rho-step-size)). OSQP's defaults are probably internally consistent, but we modified some of the default parameters to match CVXR ([here](https://cvxr.rbind.io/cvxr_examples/cvxr_solver-parameters#osqp)); this includes a tighter tolerance for convergence.

As a result, this parameter is sometimes not updated in situations where the update is required for convergence (e.g. #7). The solution (with no adverse consequences that we could find) is to force the parameter to be updated every 25 iterations in the internal OSQP algorithm (25 is the current OSQP default if the time-based switch is activated early; see [here](https://github.com/osqp/osqp/blob/1a2f2d32e3f68297f9bf4d8b8dca5cc29378eccc/include/constants.h#L82) and [here](https://github.com/osqp/osqp/blob/1a2f2d32e3f68297f9bf4d8b8dca5cc29378eccc/src/osqp.c#L461-L478)).

